# Local container env, written by SLOP's install.sh into the compose dir (the SSO
# shared secret, the gateway trust flag, the base path). Untracked, it made
# `git status --porcelain` dirty, and the updater refuses to pull a dirty checkout
# — so every install permanently blocked its own updates ("the checkout has local
# changes — resolve them on the host first"). It also holds a secret, which has no
# business sitting one `git add -A` away from a commit.
.env
